#, no-c-format
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "Who made this game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The kdegames team. You can find their website <ulink url=\"http://games.kde."
"org\">here</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where can I get cheatcodes?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "You cannot get cheatcodes for &kde; games."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I start a new game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; will load a default layout automaticly one once you start the "
"application and you can start playing right away."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I start a totaly new game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To start a new game you can either use a <link linkend=\"game-menu-new"
"\">shortcut key</link>, or a <link linkend=\"game-menu-new\">menubar</link> "
"option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid "I did something very wrong! Can I restart the game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To restart the current game you can either use a <link linkend=\"game-"
"menu-restart\">shortcut key</link>, or a <link linkend=\"game-menu-restart"
"\">menubar</link> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I pause the game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To pause the current game you may either use the <link linkend=\"game-menu-"
"pause\">toolbar</link>, a <link linkend=\"game-menu-pause\">shortcut key</"
"link>, or a <link linkend=\"game-menu-pause\">menubar</link> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to change the way this game looks. Can I?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To change the way &kappname; looks use the <link linkend=\"game-"
"settings-settings\">menubar</link> to open the <link linkend=\"configuration"
"\">configuration utility</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "I have made a mistake. Can I undo?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To undo your move you can either use a <link linkend=\"move-menu-undo"
"\">shortcut key</link>, or a <link linkend=\"move-menu-undo\">menubar</link> "
"option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "I have mistakenly undone a good move, can I redo it?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To Redo your move you can either use a <link linkend=\"move-menu-redo"
"\">shortcut key</link>, or a <link linkend=\"move-menu-redo\">menubar</link> "
"option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use keyboard?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "No. This game does not feature a keyboard play mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "I cannot figure out what to do here! Are there hints?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To use &kappname; hint feature can either use a <link linkend=\"move-"
"menu-hint\">shortcut key</link>, or a <link linkend=\"move-menu-hint"
"\">menubar</link> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I have to quit the game now, but I am not finished yet. Can I save my "
"progress?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid "No. This game does not feature a <quote>Save</quote> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where are the high scores?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To open the high scores dialog you can either use a <link linkend=\"game-"
"menu-highscores\">shortcut key</link>, or a <link linkend=\"game-menu-"
"highscores\">menubar</link> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to change the game configuration. Where do I go?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To open the <link linkend=\"configuration\">configuration utility</link> use "
"the <link linkend=\"game-settings-settings\">menubar->Settings</link> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid "I want to change the toolbar layout. What do I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the default toolbar layout use the <link linkend=\"settings-menu-"
"toolbar\"><menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"Toolbars...</guimenuitem></menuchoice></link> option in the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting the <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure "
"&kappname;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item will open a configuration "
"dialog which lets you alter the behavior of the game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kappname; configuration dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kappname; configuration dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gravity"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Checking this makes the game even harder: If a tile is removed, all tiles "
"lying above it will fall down one step."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allow unsolvable games"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, you run the risk of being presented with games that are "
"impossible to solve. Note: Even when not checked, you will fail to complete "
"a game if you remove the tiles in the wrong order!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use Chinese style: any flower matches any flower, any season match any season"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the traditional rules for matching the tiles. Previous version of "
"&kappname; used to allow only exact tiles matches, which is inconsistent "
"with Mah-jongg rules. It is recommended to keep this option checked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tiles can slide, but you can connect only in 2 lines instead of 3"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option changes the rules to the point where it almost becomes a "
"completely different game. When it is active, you can only remove the tiles "
"if they can be connected by a line consiting of only two segments instead of "
"the customary three. However, you are allowed to slide the tiles on the "
"board, if the row or column where they are placed has some empty space. To "
"make a sliding move, you have to click on the tile containing the column or "
"row that can slide, and then on the matching tile. If there are two possible "
"sliding moves, you will have to click on one of the two connecting lines to "
"chose your preferred move."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid "Board Difficulty"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The slider controls the difficulty of the board from <guilabel>Easy</"
"guilabel> to <guilabel>Hard</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "Piece Removal Speed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:468
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Adjusting this slider alters the speed at which the pieces are removed from "
"the screen after a match has been made."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tile Size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:474
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This slider allows you to can change the number of tiles on the board. The "
"more tiles you have, the harder (and longer) the game will be."
msgstr ""

